{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-38866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $T:V\\to W$ is a linear map and $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{3})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-38866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $C.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 8 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-38866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f7c5de47d4a3cc1a6dab8802044cb5ed1787b8895fcf1edc03d9afdd2a230e21"} {"question" "q-38866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-38866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 8 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 8 \\\\ 6 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & -3 \\\\ -8 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-38866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 8 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-38528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $T:V\\to W$ is a linear map and $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$\\,$ $T({b}_{1})={c}_{1}-{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=2{c}_{2}-{c}_{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-38528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write the images of vectors in $B$ relative to the basis $C:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1})={c}_{1}-{c}_{2}+{c}_{3} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2})=2{c}_{2}-{c}_{3} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix  whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and  $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-38528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f7c5de47d4a3cc1a6dab8802044cb5ed1787b8895fcf1edc03d9afdd2a230e21"} {"question" "q-38528" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-38528" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-38528" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-140430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $T:V\\to W$ is a linear map and $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{3})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-140430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $C.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-140430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f7c5de47d4a3cc1a6dab8802044cb5ed