my/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-38529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write the images of vectors in $B$ relative to the basis $C:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1})=-2{c}_{1}+4{c}_{2}-2{c}_{3} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2})=3{c}_{2}-7{c}_{3}+{c}_{1} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and  $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-38529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f7c5de47d4a3cc1a6dab8802044cb5ed1787b8895fcf1edc03d9afdd2a230e21"} {"question" "q-38529" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-38529" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4 \\\\ -7 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-38529" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-38530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $T:V\\to W$ is a linear map and $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{3})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-38530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $C.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-38530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f7c5de47d4a3cc1a6dab8802044cb5ed1787b8895fcf1edc03d9afdd2a230e21"} {"question" "q-38530" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-38530" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-38530" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-140441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ of the vector space $V$ and the basis $C$ of ${R}^{2}$ given by\n\n$$\nC={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nFind the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T:V\\to {R}^{2}$ relative to these bases if \n\n$$\nT({b}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,T({b}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-140441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nFirst, we need to find the coordinates of $T({b}_{i})$ relative to the basis $C$ for each $i=1,2.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the following matrix:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the right-hand side gives the matrix of the linear transformation relative to the bases $B$ and $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-140441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f7c5de47d4a3cc1a6dab8802044cb5ed1787b8895fcf1edc03d9afdd2a230e21"} {"question" "q-140441" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-140441" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}6 & -8 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-140441" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-97572" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ of the vector space $V$ and the basis $C$ of ${R}^{2}$ given by\n\n$$\nC={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nFind the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T:V\\to {R}^{2}$ relative to these bases if \n\n$$\nT({b}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,T({b}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-97572" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nFirst, we need to find the coordinates of $T({b}_{i})$ relative to the basis $C$ for each $i=1,2.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the following matrix:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -5 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -11 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the right-hand side gives the matrix of the linear transformation relative to the bases $B$ and $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 12 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/stat