e of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}=-4 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-97584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f7c5de47d4a3cc1a6dab8802044cb5ed1787b8895fcf1edc03d9afdd2a230e21"} {"question" "q-97584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-97584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-97584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-97588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ (shown above) and a basis $C$ of ${R}^{3}.$\nThe matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to these bases, and the vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ are also given. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-97588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can find the coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-97588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f7c5de47d4a3cc1a6dab8802044cb5ed1787b8895fcf1edc03d9afdd2a230e21"} {"question" "q-97588" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-97588" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-97588" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-140446" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ (shown above) and a basis $C$ of ${R}^{3}.$\nThe matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to these bases, and the vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ are also given. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-140446" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can find the coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}=-15 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}=30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 9 & -15 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 30\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 30\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 15\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 20 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 80 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-140446" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f7c5de47d4a3cc1a6dab8802044cb5ed1787b8895fcf1edc03d9afdd2a230e21"} {"question" "q-140446" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-140446" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 76 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 80 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 80 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 80 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-140446" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 80 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-97583" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ (shown above) and a basis $C$ of ${R}^{3}.$\nThe matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to these bases, and the vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ are also given. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-97583" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can find the coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2}=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-97583" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f7c5de47d4a3cc1a6dab8802044cb5ed1787b8895fcf1edc03d9afdd2a230e21"} {"question" "q-97583" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-97583" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-97583" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-97587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ (shown above) and a basis $C$ of ${R}^{3}.$\nThe matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to these bases, and the vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ are also given. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-97587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can find the coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -7 & 6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-97587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f7c5de47d4a3cc1a6dab8802044cb5ed1787b8895fcf1edc03d9afdd2a230e21"} {"question" "q-97587" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-97587" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-19 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "q-97587" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e07baae1835d359b8826d64709546efbcadeebe234fecb72049908b235f14ab"} {"question" "e-8604" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $\\mathbf{T} : V \\rightarrow W$ is a linear map and $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1,\\mathbf{b}_2, \\mathbf{b}_3 \\}$ and $\\mathcal{C} = \\{ \\mathbf{c}_1,\\mathbf{c}_2 \\}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. Find the matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ of the map $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_1)=-3\\mathbf{c}_1+5\\mathbf{c}_2,\\quad$ $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_2)=\\mathbf{c}_2-2\\mathbf{c}_1\\quad$ and $\\quad\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_3)=\\mathbf{c}_1+5\\mathbf{c}_2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/example-8604.json" "file_sha256" "c99d4b6ae707163a0eae5546d537ce242ef52c8e9b9080c9377007aee3e01b37"} {"question" "e-8604" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write the images of vectors in $\\mathcal{B}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C} \\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1})=-3{c}_{1}+5{c}_{2} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2})={c}_{2}-2{c}_{1} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{3})={c}_{1}+5{c}_{2} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{3})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_1),$ $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_2)$ and $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_3)$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/215cd69925ccfeab3ccb20874b7cdc2d837b99f33d8112f95fa5d2b646a27d40.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/example-8604.json" "file_sha256" "c99d4b6ae707163a0eae5546d537ce242ef52c8e9b9080c9377007aee3e01b37"} {"question" "e-8605" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2, \\mathbf{b}_3\\}$ of the vector space $V$ and the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/7c123e6f7d842a8e86e4c99826d25df070982514960752a25481a9f3f046cc1b.png)\n\nFind the matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ of the map $\\mathbf{T}:V \\to \\mathbb{R}^2$ relative to these bases if \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/9a469219c661453d7891935b2ef0a32bff972bcf903d641ca7e31b7bec26369a.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/example-8605.json" "file_sha256" "d283edfbc8349531b0cf245f45a25ad80e3bda608d22dd09673e4243074d94ac"} {"question" "e-8605" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_1),$ $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_2),$ and $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_3)$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}.$\n\nFirst, we need to find the coordinates of $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_i)$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ for each $i=1,2,3.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the following matrix:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/9d774b5bd79f14bc31e88a649fcb2a682d94ae3dd8acde5e25f52369c136e11e.png)\n\nWe reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 1 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 & 3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 & 3 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -8 & 8\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 11 & -29 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -8 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the right-hand side gives the matrix of the linear transformation relative to the bases $\\mathcal{B}$ and $\\mathcal{C} \\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/778f179c4681bcdcc5a64bcd128d946a272fa869289d2c2e542df75ad05850b6.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/example-8605.json" "file_sha256" "d283edfbc8349531b0cf245f45a25ad80e3bda608d22dd09673e4243074d94ac"} {"question" "e-5521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/7d82125089d15dada1be4f8d6669b5e125da921019b3a9d27376353dcf59a090.png)\n\nSuppose $\\mathcal{B}$ and $\\mathcal{C}$ are bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. The matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ of the linear map $\\mathbf{T}:V \\rightarrow W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x} \\in V$ relative to $\\mathcal{B}$ are shown above. Find $[\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{x})]_{\\mathcal{C}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/example-5521.json" "file_sha256" "c238ce277dfc49fdb0244720ef4330bfc3e1a15b2454381276df19466acd4192"} {"question" "e-5521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The coordinates of the image of $\\mathbf{x}$ under $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/example-5521.json" "file_sha256" "c238ce277dfc49fdb0244720ef4330bfc3e1a15b2454381276df19466acd4192"} {"question" "e-5522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/8caf13cdbf21ddfb1a121ede6ec0c21da155065905547bbd86b0e52cd57141da.png)\n\nConsider the basis $\\mathcal{B}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ (shown above) and a basis $\\mathcal{C}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^3.$\nThe matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ of the linear map $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^2 \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}^3$ relative to these bases, and the vector $\\mathbf{x} \\in \\mathbb{R}^2,$ are also given. Find $[\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{x})]_{\\mathcal{C}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/example-5522.json" "file_sha256" "3e66d86d81e876d46b7d0d4f83987b631d5bdaba830deeca085c02f1b7db5cfd"} {"question" "e-5522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can find the coordinates of the image of $\\mathbf{x}$ under $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}},$ the coordinates of $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to $\\mathcal{B}.$ So, let\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/a5b6f5f41dffd99a885bb872eac6f1e6a24bd604b360256194a0bf16b32ef381.png)\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 4 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -18\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/862742d57ad0ae4b56d6f345d825313bebf0d712f9c59ea1ed8b55d0a2eea22e.png)\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/example-5522.json" "file_sha256" "3e66d86d81e876d46b7d0d4f83987b631d5bdaba830deeca085c02f1b7db5cfd"} {"question" "q-38529" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "e9020465f0f010bb81932abaf19f5ca3eb772fe6bcf0be9ff95eaab354dfc86d" 